g comparison because now summaries are everywhere. Now, Claw can summarize, CHP can summarize, Gemini can summarize. Now, the real question is where does all the information come from? Now, Notebook LM understands documents incredibly well, whereas HappyCribe understands conversations and those are two completely different workflows. [music] Now, let's say you're researching a legal case. Notebookm is fantastic for this. When you're working from reports, [music] PDFs, evidence, academic papers, this is exactly what it was designed for. Now, imagine you're running a consulting business. Every week, you're going to be speaking with clients, taking discovery calls, running workshops, meeting with your team, interviewing customers. Your most valuable information isn't going to be sitting [music] inside PDFs. It's sitting inside conversations. And unless you're capturing those conversations, they completely disappear. And that's the problem Happy Scribe is solving for you. Then there's MCP. Honestly, I think peopl    ... [846 more chars]

